ttps://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/events/313734373/","description":"Cet événement comporte des frais de 3 $ afin de compenser le coût de l'hébergement sur la plateforme Meetup.\nThis event has a 3$ fee to help offset the cost of hosting on the Meetup platform.\n**[PAYER ICI PAY HERE](https://www.paypal.com/ncp/payment/KSPACXU2YRG66)**\n\nBonjour tout le monde!\nSoyez des nôtres au prochain French meetup au Madison Pub. Venez passer une soirée conviviale et rencontrer des francophones et francophiles de Toronto et du GTA. Tout le monde est le bienvenu peu importe votre niveau.\n\nC'est une excellente occasion de parler en français à Toronto. Nous serons au deuxième étage. La réservation est sous Le French Meetup de Toronto.\n\nSi vous ne souhaitez pas que votre photo soit publiée sur le site Meetup, veuillez informer Pierre.\n\nMerci,\nChristopher et Lemonte\n\n**Pourquoi ces frais de 3$?** Pour compenser le coût de l'hébergement sur la plate-forme Meetup de l’année courante et des années précédentes. Nous vous demandons de payer $3.00 à chaque événement. Christopher et Lemonte seront présents pour recueillir vos contributions. Nous vous prions de bien vouloir apporter de la monnaie.\nVous pouvez payer en ligne sur ce lien:[ ](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)[PAYER ICI](https://www.paypal.com/ncp/payment/KSPACXU2YRG66)\nSi vous préférez, vous pouvez payer par Interac à cette adresse: pierrotgilbert@gmail.com\n...............................................................................................................................\nHello everyone!\nJoin us for the next French Meetup at the Madison Pub!\nEnjoy a friendly evening and meet Francophones and Francophiles from Toronto and the GTA. Everyone is welcome, no matter your level.\nThis is a great opportunity to speak French right here in Toronto. We will be on the second floor, and the reservation is under *Le French Meetup de Toronto*.\nIf you prefer not to have your photo posted on the Meetup website, please inform Pierre.\nThank you,\nChristopher and Lemonte\n\nWhy the $3 fee?\nIt helps cover the cost of hosting our group on the Meetup platform — not only for this year, but also for previous years. We kindly ask everyone to contribute $3.00 at each event. Christopher and Lemonte will be there to collect your contributions, so please try to bring exact change.\nYou can also pay online using this link:[ ](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)[PAY HERE](https://www.paypal.com/ncp/payment/KSPACXU2YRG66)\nIf you prefer, you can pay via Interac at this address: pierrotgilbert@gmail.com\n\nVotre soutien est grandement apprécié ! 😊\nYour support is greatly appreciated!","startDate":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Madison Avenue Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"14 Madison Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"[女性限定] Girls’ Night🇨🇦🇯🇵Language Exchange [CAS]🦄🌱","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/events/316362361/","description":"⚠️日本語の案内は下にあります⚠️\n\nWelcome to CAS Japanese x English Girl's Night, where we enjoy small group chats in both languages over tea and the occasional board game 🦄🌱\n\n🌞Perfect for you if...\n☀︎You're looking to make female friends in Toronto.☀︎You've been wanting to try a Meetup event but feel a little nervous.\n\n🎟️Admission: $10\nBring a snack or drink to share and receive 50% off (**only $5**).\nPayment: Cash or e-Transfer only\n(✉️hanano.ishida1@gmail.com)\n\n🎀We'll provide green tea, cups, paper napkins, wet wipes, plates, and board games.\n\n📍Meeting Point: Main Stage on the 1st Floor of the Library\n（If you arrive late, please come to Study Room 1 or 2, or one of the 2nd-floor study rooms.）\n\n🗒️Some House Rules\nIf you can no longer attend, please change your RSVP to \"Not Attending\".\n\nFailure to do so twice may result in removal from the group.\n\n🧸Participation Policy\nThis event is limited to individuals who were assigned female at birth (AFAB).\n\nIf it is at all unclear for us whether you meet this criteria, we reserve the right to remove your RSVP without explanation.\n\nCAS Japanese x English Girl's Nightへようこそ🦄🌱\nおしゃべり、お菓子、お茶、ボードゲームを楽しみながら、日本語と英語の少人数グループで交流する女性限定イベントです♡\n\n🌞こんな方におすすめ\n☀︎トロントで女性の友達を作りたい方\n☀︎Meetupイベントに参加してみたいけれど少し不安がある方\n\n🎟️参加費：10ドル\nお菓子や飲み物をシェア用に持参すると\n参加費が半額の**5ドル**！\n\nお支払い方法：現金またはE-Transferのみ\n(✉️hanano.ishida1@gmail.com)\n\n🎀 緑茶、紙コップ、紙ナプキン、ウェットティッシュ、紙皿、ボードゲームはこちらでご用意しています。\n\n📍集合場所：図書館1階 メインステージ\n（遅れて来られる場合はStudy Room 1 or 2、もしくは2階のスタディルームまで！）\n\n🗒️ご参加にあたってのお願い\n参加できなくなった場合は、必ずRSVPを「Not Attending（欠席）」へ変更してください。\n無断欠席（RSVPを変更しないまま欠席）が2回あった場合は、グループから退会していただく場合があります。\n\n🧸参加条件\nこのイベントは、出生時に女性として割り当てられた方（AFAB：Assigned Female At Birth)を対象としています。\n参加条件を満たしているか判断が難しい場合は、主催者の判断により、事前の説明なくRSVPを取り消す場合があります。","startDate":"2026-11-10T23:50:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Reference Library","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"789 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CAS Meetup Community","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/"},"performer":"CAS Meetup Community"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Founders, Investors & Talent Networking Mixer | Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-networking-founder-ecosystem-toronto/events/316406722/","description":"Join founders, investors and tech talent at this curated **startup networking event in Toronto.**\n\nMeet ambitious builders, exchange ideas and discover new opportunities in a dynamic community environment.\n\n**RSVP: [Use this link](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/startup-networking-toronto-founders-investors-talent-mixer-tickets-1987710363204?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true)**\n**Please note that RSVP is managed via Eventbrite to control attendee lists — don’t ignore it to avoid issues with on-site payment.**\n\n**💡 Why This Event Is Different**\nMost networking events end with exchanged LinkedIn profiles.\nThis one focuses on real conversations and real opportunities.\nWe bring together founders, investors, engineers, operators and talent in a curated environment designed to create meaningful connections.\nThrough interactive networking rounds, open conversations and pitch opportunities, participants can share challenges, exchange insights and build relationships that last beyond the event.\n\n**🤝 What to Expect**\n\n* **Interactive Networking**\n\nStructured networking rounds where participants briefly introduce themselves, share current challenges and explore collaboration opportunities.\n\n* **Talent Corner**\n\nRecruiters and hiring managers can briefly share open positions, while engineers and operators can introduce their skills and interests.\n\n* **Startup Conversations**\n\nOpen discussions about fundraising, product development, growth and startup challenges.\n\n**👥 Who Should Attend**\n\n• Startup founders\n• Investors and angels\n• Engineers and builders\n• Operators and product managers\n• Recruiters and HR professionals\n• Sales and business development professionals\n• Job seekers interested in startups\n• Newcomers to the Toronto tech ecosystem","startDate":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Blood Brothers Brewing","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"165 Geary Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Startup Networking & Founder Ecosystem | Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-networking-founder-ecosystem-toronto/"},"performer":"Startup Networking & Founder Ecosystem | Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI & Tech Networking Event in Toronto by Ascent Valley","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-networking-founder-ecosystem-toronto/events/316406793/","description":"Join founders, investors and tech talent at this curated **startup networking event in Toronto.**\n\nMeet ambitious builders, exchange ideas and discover new opportunities in a dynamic community environment.\n\n**RSVP: [Use this link](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ai-tech-networking-event-in-toronto-by-ascent-valley-tickets-1999720403558?aff=oddtdtcreator)**\n**Please note that RSVP is managed via Eventbrite to control attendee lists — don’t ignore it to avoid issues with on-site payment.**\n\n**🚀 Meet investors, founders, AI experts, operators, and immigrant entrepreneurs building the next generation of global companies.**\n\n* Share your project and get feedback.\n* Connect with capital.\n* Expand your network.\n* This is where conversations turn into partnerships.\n* Use our participant mini app to keep every contact and insight from the event — nothing gets lost.\n\n👥 Who You’ll Meet\n• Startup Founders\n• Angel Investors & VC firms\n• AI Experts\n• Entrepreneurs from Europe, Asia & the UK\n• Marketers, Sales leaders & Business Advisors\n• Builders & Game Changers\n\nStartup Pitch Session\nSelected founders take the stage for a focused 5-minute presentation in front of active investors and tech leaders.\nEach startup receives:\n⚡ Professional evaluation\n⚡ Investor feedback\n⚡ Visibility inside our global ecosystem\n\n**Why You Can’t Miss It**\n• Meet Tech & Business professionals, founders, and active investors\n• Gain real feedback from venture capitalists and angel investors\n• Discover new opportunities in AI, Tech & early-stage startups\n• Build meaningful connections in a global entrepreneurial community\nIf you’re serious about startups — you should be in the room.\n\n📈 Want to Pitch?\nSend your deck to:\n📧 events@ascentvalley.club or fill [form](https://ascentvalley.com/pitch)\nLimited spots. Curated selection.\n\n🏆 The startup recognized as “Most Investment-Worthy” will be featured across our social media and included in our investor newsletter.\n\n**🌟 About Ascent Valley**\n\n[Ascent Valley ](https://ascentvalley.com/infrastructure \"https://ascentvalley.com/infrastructure\")is a global ecosystem connecting founders, innovators, and investors.\nWe believe great ideas shouldn’t stay hidden — they deserve to be heard, challenged, and supported by the right people.\nOur mission is to create environments where ambitious builders connect, collaborate, and grow together.","startDate":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Blood Brothers Brewing","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"165 Geary Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Startup Networking & Founder Ecosystem | Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-networking-founder-ecosystem-toronto/"},"performer":"Startup Networking & Founder Ecosystem | Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tools to Run Your Business","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-public-library-small-business-networking-meetup/events/316714478/","description":"For new business owners, staying organized can be just as challenging to find customers. This session will explore the tools that can take routine work off your plate. From bookkeeping and invoicing, to scheduling, payments, customer records, marketing, and social media creation. We will also look at where AI tools can genuinely help save time and add value versus making unnecessary work. We'll discover where to find free resources, and how to avoid subscribing to services that won't be of value in the long run. You'll leave with a concise list of tools appropriate for new business owners.\n\nThe program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\n\nPresented by Ryan Knight, TPL's 2026 [Entrepreneur in Residence](https://tpl.ca/programs-and-classes/featured/entrepreneur-in-residence/) (EIR) at Toronto Reference Library.\n\n**Registration via TPL website:** [https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31)\n**Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.**\n\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: [tpl.ca/accessibility-events](https://tpl.ca/accessibility/accessibility-supports/programs-and-events/?_gl=1*v83hy7*_ga*NDk5MDg2NTE1LjE3NjYwMDgxODQ.*_ga_G99DMMNG39*czE3NjkxMDY3NDMkbzE0JGcxJHQxNzY5MTA2ODM0JGozOCRsMCRoMA..).","startDate":"2026-11-10T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Public Library - Toronto Reference Library","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON M4W 2G8, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-public-library-small-business-networking-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"ABCD Reads Body Language by Meg Howrey","url":"https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/events/316295954/","description":"ABCD Reads ***[Body Language](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4801989)*** by Meg Howrey.\n([RESULTS](https://opavote.com/results/6325601387675648) of the poll for this event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n\"Sloane, a former actress now working as a therapist, is determined to find a meaningful way through menopause, away from marketing schemes, possibly with the aid of psychedelics. Her sister Laurel is managing her own growing rage and restlessness while engaging in work at an environmental non-profit and raising teenagers. Nanette, the youngest, has answered a long-delayed religious calling and is living as a Novice in a convent. All three lives will be further disrupted when Sloane receives a call summoning her to their mother’s house, Laurel discovers possible evidence of her husband’s infidelity, and Nanette finds herself in the middle of a media frenzy after a spontaneous act of public prayer.\nSoon, all three are reunited under their mother’s roof, and no one can seem to agree about anything beyond the Barbara has dementia, as did her mother and sister before her. Will it be an opportunity for the closed door of their very private mother’s inner life to crack open? A lesson in care; a shared responsibility that will be the making of this family, divided by large age gaps, parental divorce, and temperament? Or will a stunning revelation upend not only their mother’s remaining time, but divide the sisters permanently?\nWith razor-sharp prose and undeniable humor, acclaimed author Meg Howrey brings an American family in the midst of a painful crisis to unforgettable life, interrogating memory and emotional inheritance, the right of a woman’s autonomy, and the indelible bonds even the most disparate of sisters can share.\" (from [Goodreads](https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/244709885-body-language))\n\n\"Howrey is a reliably beautiful stylist, and her slyly funny prose and blade-sharp insights into human behavior really should put her in the same conversation as writers like Ann Patchett and Barbara Kingsolver. Though this novel hits some familiar beats, Howrey manages to haul in plenty of shimmering pearls on the perils and joys of womanhood—whatever that means.\nA comfort meal of a novel: poignant and prismatic.\" (from [Kirkus](https://www.kirkusreviews.com/book-reviews/meg-howrey/body-language-4/))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arrive 30 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterward to connect with other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you have read the book before attending (though finishing any book is not a barrier to participating, as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time attendees can join for free. If the event is full, we maintain an unofficial waitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/55295192/) a direct message for more information, in either case.\n\nWe request a $3 contribution from regular attendees to help cover our monthly meetup costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event, we will ask for nominees for our next book. If you have a good one in mind, please ensure it is between 200-400 pages long, available from the Toronto Public Library, and counts as contemporary literary fiction (though these are not hard and fast rules). When enough nominees are collected, Michael will send the members a direct message with a link where you can vote.","startDate":"2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Bar Wellington","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"520 Wellington Street W., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"A Book Club, Downtown (ABCD)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/"},"performer":"A Book Club, Downtown (ABCD)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Pickering Indoor Soccer","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-soccer-meetup/events/316586934/","description":"**🚨IMPORTANT UPDATE - READ BEFORE RSVPing🚨**\n\nWe’ve launched our new website: www.soccertoronto.ca **All sign‑ups must now be completed through the website.** Meetup reservations **do NOT** confirm your spot.\nThere is **no texting or emailing to sign up anymore.** All program information, registration, rules, and updates are now on the website.\n**Do NOT show up without signing up in advance — you will be turned away.**\n\n**HOW TO SIGN UP**\n👉 Register online at www.soccertoronto.ca\n👉 Payments must be sent to payment@soccertoronto.ca\n👉 For general questions only, email info@soccertoronto.ca\n\n**TORONTO’S BEST INDOOR PICKUP SOCCER**\nHosted by **Soccer Toronto** — Est. 2008\n\n**FALL/WINTER SCHEDULE**\n\n* **Tuesdays** — 10:30 PM to 12:00 AM\n\nPickup soccer runs weekly at **Pickering Soccer Centre**, **80 Conlin Road W, Oshawa, ON L1G 7W1 (Simcoe St N & Conlin Road W)**.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/A8L6WDP7CCWk2aYY6\n\nWe welcome skilled regulars and new players every week. There is always a game.\n\n**PROGRAM DETAILS**\n\n* **Format:** 8v8 - 2 Fields - 5 Teams Max\n* **Level:** All players welcome (Beginner to Advanced